.SH NAME
mouser\-model \- Model providers (OpenAI\-compatible, Anthropic, Google, local); see docs/models.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser model\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Model providers (OpenAI\-compatible, Anthropic, Google, local); see docs/models.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mouser\-model\-list(1)
List providers (built\-in, configured, plugins) and their models; * marks the default
.TP
mouser\-model\-add(1)
Add or update: `add openai \-\-key\-stdin`, `add grok \-\-key\-stdin` (grok_… or xai\-… key) or `add grok \-\-desktop`, or `add NAME \-\-api openai|anthropic|google \-\-url URL [\-\-model M]…`. Without \-\-model it lists the provider\*(Aqs models and asks
.TP
mouser\-model\-remove(1)
Remove a configured provider and its key
.TP
mouser\-model\-test(1)
Stream one reply from PROVIDER[/MODEL] (default: the default model)
.TP
mouser\-model\-default(1)
Set the default model: PROVIDER[/MODEL]
.TP
mouser\-model\-local(1)
The built\-in local model (gemma\-local): status, download, delete, url, dir
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
